            <ArticleTitle>Coronary spasm and cardiac arrest from carcinoid crisis during laser bronchoscopy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>598-600</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bronchoscopic manipulation of an endobronchial carcinoid can precipitate a carcinoid crisis. Coronary artery spasm is an uncommon manifestation of carcinoid crisis, and has never been reported as a complication of flexible bronchoscopy. We report a case of a 10-year-old girl who developed coronary artery spasm and cardiac arrest during neodymiumyttrium aluminum garnet (Nd-YAG) laser photoresection of an endobronchial carcinoid. Recognition of this unusual presentation of a carcinoid crisis is important as the treatment approach differs from standard resuscitation protocols.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
